  "result": {
    "summary": "All four review comments are addressed. The `since` test now makes two commits after the merge-base and asserts ahead 2 without `since` and ahead 1 with it. The None cases cover an existing non-git tempdir, a patched `_git_in` returning returncode=1, the nonexistent path, and per-command OSError and TimeoutExpired. `parse_porcelain_z` yields both rename endpoints, the docstring explains why, and the parity test scope includes old/name.txt. `_resolve_base` takes an optional timeout and keeps the old call shape when it is None. `execute_outcome` calls `head_sha` before and after status and returns None if HEAD moved. `gitutil` does not import `daemon`, and changes stay within the two scoped files. I ran `tests/test_gitutil.py` in the T-1490 worktree: 6 tests pass. I did not run `tests-green.sh`.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/gitutil.py",
        "line": 57,
        "issue": "`since` is passed unvalidated into the `rev-list` range string `{since}..HEAD`. A caller-supplied value starting with `-` could be read as an option. The caller is internal, so the risk is low. A `--end-of-options` guard or a hex check would harden it, but that is outside the four requested fixes.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
